# Security (non-negotiable)

Read `docs/SECURITY.md` before touching headers, iframes, forms, private content or dependencies.

## Never

- Put a secret, token or password in front code, Git, or `.env.example` values (`VITE_*` = public)
- Put the jury password anywhere but the Netlify env var; put PDFs outside `public/jury/fiches/`; import jury text into TS/JSON
- Use a client-side password, JS check or hidden URL as an access control
- Use `innerHTML` with dynamic content (XSS); add inline `<script>`/`style=""` (CSP)
- Add `frame-src https:` or any third-party script CDN
- Publish raw client data (Vill’âge Jeunes) or SAE credentials (Lab Horizon)
- Re-add Supabase / app auth (removed 2026-10-21) without a new decision in `docs/SECURITY.md` §0

## Always

- **Delivery (locked 2026-10-21):** one Netlify site; public pages open; `/jury` (pages + PDFs) behind server-side Basic-Auth from env `JURY_BASIC_AUTH`, injected by `scripts/inject-jury-auth.mjs` (`docs/SECURITY.md` §0, `docs/content/teacher-site.md`). GitHub repo private.
- Keep `public/_headers` strict; a new iframe origin goes in `frame-src` **and** in `tests/feature/catalog-and-headers.test.ts`
- `npm run gate` green before done; `npm run audit:prod` before deploy

If a task weakens security, **stop** and update `docs/SECURITY.md` first.
